{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"116219","commit":"0cff8dbc0d3b90873f1cde6b09283ae47b9273ab","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `invokeRollover` method now takes a `Runnable runAfter` instead of an `AtomicBoolean creationCheck`. This change is logical given the new usage pattern, but ensure that all call sites correctly pass a `Runnable` that sets the `creationCheck` to false or performs other necessary actions. Verify that this change does not introduce any unintended side effects in the calling methods.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java-x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java-38611:38624,38625:38638,38734:40591-38443:38567,38737:38745,38746:38754,38850:40602","promptId":"#89V9Z","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":38611,"endPos":38624,"startLine":791,"startLineOffset":14,"endLine":791,"endLineOffset":27,"length":14},{"pos":38625,"endPos":38638,"startLine":791,"startLineOffset":28,"endLine":791,"endLineOffset":41,"length":14},{"pos":38734,"endPos":40591,"startLine":794,"startLineOffset":31,"endLine":832,"endLineOffset":9,"length":1858}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":38443,"endPos":38567,"startLine":787,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":790,"endLineOffset":7,"length":125},{"pos":38737,"endPos":38745,"startLine":795,"startLineOffset":14,"endLine":795,"endLineOffset":22,"length":9},{"pos":38746,"endPos":38754,"startLine":795,"startLineOffset":23,"endLine":795,"endLineOffset":31,"length":9},{"pos":38850,"endPos":40602,"startLine":798,"startLineOffset":31,"endLine":838,"endLineOffset":9,"length":1753}]}]},{"comment":"The logic introduced in the diff aims to handle cases where `indexTemplate` might not yet exist in the cluster state or has a lower priority than another template matching the data stream. However, there is a potential issue with the null check for `dsTemplateName`. If `MetadataIndexTemplateService.findV2Template(metadata, ds.getName(), ds.isHidden())` returns `null`, the subsequent line `final ComposableIndexTemplate dsTemplate \u003d metadata.templatesV2().get(dsTemplateName);` will throw a `NullPointerException` because `dsTemplateName` would be `null`.\nTo fix this, you should add a null check for `dsTemplateName` before attempting to retrieve `dsTemplate` from `metadata.templatesV2()`. Here is the suggested change:\n```java\nfinal String dsTemplateName \u003d MetadataIndexTemplateService.findV2Template(metadata, ds.getName(), ds.isHidden());\nif (templateName.equals(dsTemplateName)) {\n    return true;\n}\n// findV2Template did not match templateName, which implies one of two things:\n// - indexTemplate has a lower priority than the index template matching for ds, OR\n// - indexTemplate does not yet exist in cluster state (i.e. because it\u0027s in the process of being\n// installed or updated)\n//\n// Because of the second case, we must check if indexTemplate\u0027s priority is greater than the matching\n// index template, in case it would take precedence after installation/update.\nif (dsTemplateName \u003d\u003d null) {\n    return true; // Assuming that if no template matches, indexTemplate should be considered a match\n}\nfinal ComposableIndexTemplate dsTemplate \u003d metadata.templatesV2().get(dsTemplateName);\nreturn dsTemplate \u003d\u003d null || indexTemplate.priorityOrZero() \u003e dsTemplate.priorityOrZero();\n```","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java-x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java-42540:42643-42551:43598","promptId":"#KXMMK","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":42540,"endPos":42643,"startLine":870,"startLineOffset":26,"endLine":870,"endLineOffset":129,"length":104}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":42551,"endPos":43598,"startLine":876,"startLineOffset":26,"endLine":890,"endLineOffset":13,"length":1048}]}]},{"comment":"The method name change from `applyRolloverAfterTemplateV2Upgrade` to `applyRolloverAfterTemplateV2Update` is inconsistent with the comment update in `#K9N06`. The comment mentions \"updated, including its initial installation,\" which implies a broader scope than just an upgrade. However, the method name change suggests it only covers updates and not installations. Consider renaming the method to reflect both upgrades and installations or updating the comment to align with the current method name.\nThe method name `applyRolloverAfterTemplateV2Update` is referenced incorrectly as `applyRolloverAfterTemplateV2Upgrade`. This typo should be corrected to maintain consistency and avoid confusion.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/YamlTemplateRegistry.java-x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/YamlTemplateRegistry.java-8863:8898-8863:8897","promptId":"#BEMP8","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/YamlTemplateRegistry.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/YamlTemplateRegistry.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":8863,"endPos":8898,"startLine":230,"startLineOffset":22,"endLine":230,"endLineOffset":57,"length":36}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":8863,"endPos":8897,"startLine":230,"startLineOffset":22,"endLine":230,"endLineOffset":56,"length":35}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java-x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/templat